From 9dbbcab0a093fd713e7487b3fd2332dc217f1e12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hmty11 <darrenjeho@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:18:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] fix(agent): replay transient pre-content stream deaths

- Upstream proxies (9router/OmniRoute, custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints) sometimes close the SSE connection before any content is produced; pi-ai surfaces "Stream ended without finish_reason".
- piEngineForSpec's streamFn now replays such attempts with backoff (max 2, 1s/3s): nothing was shown or persisted, so a replay cannot duplicate transcript content.
- Failures after visible content, non-transient errors, and aborts settle immediately; a dead attempt leaks no events (start held back until real content).
- Custom routes re-resolve model metadata per attempt so a replay honours changed discovery.
- Regression suite tests/stream-retry.test.ts drives a scripted provider through the real engine seam: recovery, budget exhaustion, non-transient, post-content, abort.
---
